From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: pwm: allwinner,sun20i-d1-pwm: Add A733

The A733 has two PWM controllers, PWM0 and PWM1, with ten channels
each. They are of the generation this binding describes: the global
registers (clock configuration, clock gating, enable) and the control
and period registers of a channel are those of the D1. The registers of
channel N start at 0x100 + N * 0x40 on the A733 and at 0x100 + N * 0x20
on the D1 (A733 manual, section 18.7.7, PDF p.1332-1333). A driver that
treats the A733 as a D1 addresses the wrong registers for every channel
but the first, so the A733 gets its own compatible, without the D1
compatible as a fallback.

Each A733 controller has one interrupt line (A733 manual, section
12.2.3.1, PDF p.614). Add "interrupts" as an optional property, as the
binding describes the hardware.

Not covered: the S_PWM controller, which has other clock sources.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board; the driver binds to
PWM1 through this compatible with ten channels.

Assisted-by: LLM
